column47:
A DOM is just a tree of nodes, each of which has a fixed set of fields based on its type. That makes it automatically doable if you throw enough collections of key-value pairs at it:<p><pre><code>  # <a href="http://example.com">hello world</a>

  {
    "node-type":"element",
    "namespace":"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml",
    "name":"a",
    "attributes":[
      {
        "namespace":null,
        "name":"href",
        "value":"http://example.com"
      }
    ],
    "children":[
      {
        "node-type":"text",
        "value":"hello world"
      }
    ]
  }</code></pre>
